{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1125403-pretend-i-m-almost-totally-clueless-about-demon-the-descent","id":1125403,"title":"Pretend I'm almost totally clueless about Demon: the Descent....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-05T16:08:20-07:00","id":1125403,"title":"Pretend I'm almost totally clueless about Demon: the Descent....","content":"Okay, so I know that we've traded in God for a mysterious and enigmatic God-Machine. I know that angels are constructed servants, and that demons are angels that have deviated from their mission parameters. I know that the general mood is spy/suspense, and that the abilities Demons have are translated that way. <br /> <br /> I want to know more, because I'm curious. What endgame do Demons strive for? What are some things they run across as rebellious Angels? How do they get through the day-to-day? What are their reactions to the other cryptids running around the World of Darkness? How much supernatural bleeds through the gloss of covert-ops? What are some good sources of inspiration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T16:48:32-07:00","id":1125414,"title":"","content":"In general, the Unchained strive to pass undetected for as long as possible; many eventually build their Ciphers in the pursuit of self-knowledge and total liberation from the Machine, or at least existence on their own terms.<br /> <br /> The pervasive strangeness and fragmentation of the Machine registers to their senses, and the risks of active scanning tend to be balanced with the threat of external compromise such that over time a demon tends to be less able to manage a human life and more reliant on their ability to be multiple discrete persons and bend reality with directed application of Aether, transitioning from deep cover agent to serial fugitive as the type of rogue asset they are shifts to something more reliant on suborned Infrastructure and more likely to have room to maneuver for open negotiations with the System.<br /> <br /> As a disconnected piece of the precision-oriented engine that drives the world, the stakes and volume of Unchained operations tend to vary widely by local politics and personalities such that some demons will be more invested in living comfortably and others will have loftier ambitions \u2014 the Storyteller's Guide has an entire chapter devoted to shifting your game more toward one quarter of the genre or another, but by default the ring is the most commonplace social structure a demon will interact with.<br /> <br /> Heist stories scan fairly well to Demon's structure; the ironclad fa\u00e7ade and unique circumstances of a fallen angel lend themselves to the secret conflicts of interests that show up in such operations, and the Incarnations and Agendas both map quite readily to discrete roles like the face or the getaway driver, to say nothing of how angelic Missions prepare demons for thinking of missions in terms of process more certainly than purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T16:49:32-07:00","id":1125416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What endgame do Demons strive for? </div> </div> </div>Depends on the demon. Each is seeking a hell, but what hell means is very personal. One demon might just want to settle down to a human life. One wants immortality in a series of rich, powerful Cover identities. One wants to destroy the Machine utterly, another just to purge It from their backyard. Another wants to return to it, but on their terms.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are some things they run across as rebellious Angels? </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re not angels anymore, there are some big differences. They run into angels and other servants of the Machine \u2013 human cultists, sleeper agents and other dupes, people and animals <i>changed</i> by exposure to the Machine\u2019s supernatural pollution, rival demons, Exiles who are neither angel nor demon and even stranger things (cracks in reality leads to alternative presents/pasts/futures running parallel, the vengeful ghosts of former Cover-lives, microscopic machines that reprogram/puppeteer people, possessed/sentient buildings).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do they get through the day-to-day? </div> </div> </div>Generally in their Covers, acting in-character for their Cover-life. A demon with an office job works the office job. A demon with a homeless alcoholic for a Cover is on the streets, drinking, Except, of course, when they\u2019re spying/infiltrating/making deals for new Covers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are their reactions to the other cryptids running around the World of Darkness? </div> </div> </div>Do you mean cryptids as in animals mutated into supernatural beings as a byproduct of the Machine\u2019s workings, or things like vampires, mages and changelings? I\u2019m assuming the latter\u2026 How much crossover you want is up to you, but as perfect liars (it\u2019s mechanically impossible to tell if a demon is telling the truth or not) who can swap faces with minimal effort, they\u2019re likely to have the upper hand in most of their dealings. Beasts hate \u2018em though, they don\u2019t register as kin.<br /> <i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much supernatural bleeds through the gloss of covert-ops? </div> </div> </div></i><br /> A lot of it is presentation, but Demon: The Descent is as much supernatural as sci-fi. Demons can literally catch fire, sprout wings, possess people, animate dead bodies, kill or command with a word, drive people mad, summon swarms of insects\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are some good sources of inspiration? </div> </div> </div>Person of Interest, the Matrix. Dark City, basically <i>any</i> spy media, more sympathetic fictional demons (Vertigo\u2019s Lucifer, arguably even Paradise Lost).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 08-05-2017, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T17:03:01-07:00","id":1125418,"title":"","content":"Demons strive to Descend (title drop) into Hell. Hell is kind of a nebulous concept, though. It typically involves freedom from the God-Machine, but the specifics are highly influenced by each demon's individual philosophy as well as the broader philosophical trends as exemplified by the Agendas. Broadly speaking, Inquisitors seek freedom through enlightenment, Integrators by redeeming or returning to the God-Machine, Saboteurs by destroying the God-Machine and Tempters by building a private fief.<br /> <br /> The archetypal demon challenge is that the God-Machine is up to something and you have to stop it - either because its messing with your turf specifically or because you have a grudge against it in general. While doing so they'll primarily run into angels, cultists and other demons, plus whatever unique weirdness is relevant to this particular piece of Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> A large portion of a demon's life is spent just living a normal, human life. They eat breakfast, go to work, drink in bars. Demons are natural experts at pretending to be human. One of their inborn powers is immaculate poker face, among other things.<br /> <br /> Demons live in a world where no-one can be trusted, and are often themselves extremely untrustworthy. They see almost everyone, including other supernaturals, as pieces in the spy game. If they think someone or -thing is useful, they will attempt to manipulate it to their favor. Usually the most amicable interactions between a demon and <i>any</i> other being is an exchange of favors. Naturally this varies between individuals, but that's the general theme. (Side note: 'Cryptid' is actually a specific term in CofD which refers to animals warped by the God-Machine's presence)<br /> <br /> The supernatural definitely shines through. What makes Demon &quot;more&quot; than a spy game is the fact that they have access to extraordinary abilities. Sure there's a lot of regular legwork, and to a extent Embeds just facilitate the doing of action movie spy stuff. But the crucial difference between a demon and a spy is that when things go sideways, a demon can teleport away/command the gunman to surrender/grow impenetrable armored scales/turn into a beacon of light and fire and incinerate every enemy combatant in a four-block radius.<br /> <br /> The Americans is an interesting TV show about deep-cover Soviet agents that goes over a lot of the same ground as demon. I've heard some people say Person of Interest is basically Demon: The Show as well, but I haven't watched it myself. Burn Notice is good for a slightly sillier take on the genre. The Matrix is also an obvious inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T23:37:11-07:00","id":1125499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1125403-pretend-i-m-almost-totally-clueless-about-demon-the-descent#post1125403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so I know that we've traded in God for a mysterious and enigmatic God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey who says god is not a machine so complex we can't understand it in the first place <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T08:36:57-07:00","id":1125606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1125403-pretend-i-m-almost-totally-clueless-about-demon-the-descent?p=1125499#post1125499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey who says god is not a machine so complex we can't understand it in the first place <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The whole universe looks like an immensely complex system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}